    "summary": "The complete candidate adds S2-03c bounded customer audit dispatch to the inherited settings, sender, saved Test, capture and snapshot stack. AuditCollector admits detached revision-bound events without I/O, keeps one item and serialized-byte account through authorization, send, retry and physical settlement, and uses one fresh full saved version before each attempt. Successful activity-driven snapshot observations cancel old revisions. Hosted storage composes one shared native sender for export and saved Test; shutdown closes snapshots, queue and SQL in that order without extending the application deadline. Native sender cancellation clears its prepared payload while physical admission lasts until cleanup. System diagnostics stay separate. No new package, schema, paid resource, MFA rule, provider operation or deployment topology is added by this slice; the inherited complete-main architecture and policy impacts remain. The logging object CR remains applied: concrete SystemLogger uses distinct console/OTel SystemLogSink roles, with unchanged preparation and output behavior. DestinationSettingsService requires its sender; shared application composition supplies the same real sender to saved Test and export, and tests use explicit roles. This restack preserves the original sender lifecycle/export behavior and all prior PR238 inclusion. The current CR follow-up adds held-socket-close Buffer clearing and no-cancellation warning characterizations, and explicit Test sender stubs at read/Save/export-authorization test compositions. It preserves production source, sender ownership, and the shared saved Test/export sender.",
